Jukka Lahtinen wrote:
> The file doesn't exist in your home directory before you create it or
> copy from elsewhere.
> An example can be found in the source tree as sys/share/NetHack.cnf.
> You can copy it as .nethackrc in your home directory to begin with.
> Remember to set the permissions so that the game can read it.
> chmod a+x ~
> chmod a+r ~/.nethackrc
> (I think that will do.)

This step is unnecessary if the game is correctly installed (with setgid
games, no setuid); it should be able to read the file if the player can
read the file. (There's some workaround code that tries to make it work
even if the game is incorrectly installed, although of course in that
situation it might not necessarily work.)

